CRITERION 1 - Conflicting re-post reports the STORED verdict.  PASS
=====================================================================
Delivered test: TestHandleResolve_ConflictingRepostReportsStoredVerdict
(internal/handlers/transfers/handlers_test.go:434).

  $ go test -count=1 -run TestHandleResolve -v ./internal/handlers/transfers/
  --- PASS: TestHandleResolve_ConflictingRepostReportsStoredVerdict (0.02s)

I did not take the test's word for the message. An out-of-tree probe
(zz_probe_test.go in the scratch copy, new handlers.go in place) drove the exact
sequence - GET /transfers to seed the queue, POST confirm, dl.LoadData(), POST
reject - and logged the rendered message and the on-disk file:

  $ go test -count=1 -run TestProbe_AllPaths ./internal/handlers/transfers/ -v
  PROBE crit1 confirm: status=200
  PROBE crit1 conflicting-reject: status=200 msg="Pair 197a8e9d43a8 was already
      confirmed; the reject you just submitted was not applied."
  PROBE crit1 persisted verdict for 197a8e9d43a8 = "confirm"
  PROBE crit1 transfer_decisions.json on disk:
      { "decisions": { "197a8e9d43a8": { ... "verdict": "confirm", ... } } }

The message names the STORED verdict (confirmed), states the submitted verdict was
not applied, and data/transfer_decisions.json still holds confirm after the rejected
attempt. The delivered test asserts all four of these itself, including
`dec.Verdict != transfers.VerdictConfirm` against the reloaded decisions map
(handlers_test.go:483-496), and negatively asserts the body does NOT contain
"already rejected" (:474) nor the success wording "Rejected pair" (:477).

